# Line-ending policy
#
# Repo is checked out on both Windows (primary) and macOS (when working from
# the OneDrive-synced clone on a MacBook). Without this file, every cross-OS
# OneDrive sync flips CRLF ↔ LF on text files and produces ~12,600 fake "modifications"
# in `git status`, blocking clean pulls. See ONEDRIVE-WORKFLOW.md.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` tells git:
#   - Auto-detect text vs binary on first add
#   - Store text files with LF in the index
#   - Check text files out with LF on every platform (Windows included)
#
# Binary file types are listed explicitly so git never tries to normalize them.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary file types — explicit overrides
*.xlsx binary
*.xlsm binary
*.xls  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.tar  binary

# PowerShell scripts: keep LF too — modern PowerShell on Windows reads either.
# (No override needed; the `* text=auto eol=lf` line already covers them.)
